# S5-07 canonical initramfs same-input replay control

Date: 2026-11-16

## Purpose and scope

Repeat each run from the canonical updated-initramfs 3-billion N=2 series as
an independent direct invocation, using the exact same run-specific nonce and
guest artifact hashes. This tests whether the observed run-specific state is
repeatable under identical guest-visible input. The controls are diagnostic,
not a counted unique-nonce series and not S5-07 acceptance evidence.

Both direct invocations used the same runner binary rebuilt from commit
`b6d5e78` (SHA-256
`d0e3be4b345cb1ce4b2b5e72c721630ab098641b29e77816b13fdd2e13c4251f`), kernel,
canonical initramfs, CPU0 ACPI blob, 128 MiB RAM, 3,000,000,000 retirement
budget, `stage4a --user-mode --set-cpl0`, and schema-v5
`--execution-observations-out`. No `--linux-norandmaps` flag was used.

```sh
target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --nonce OD518e878f3f96ffdf800012fdc00000000 \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --ram-mib 128 \
  --out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0001.json \
  --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode \
  --execution-observations-out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0001-execution-observations.json

target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --nonce OD518e87a00efc97e3800012fdc00000001 \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --ram-mib 128 \
  --out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0002.json \
  --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode \
  --execution-observations-out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0002-execution-observations.json
```

## Results

| Source series run | Replayed nonce | Direct retired / stop | Stop equal | UART equal | Sidecar equal |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0001 | `OD518e878f3f96ffdf800012fdc00000000` | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | yes | yes | yes |
| 0002 | `OD518e87a00efc97e3800012fdc00000001` | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | yes | yes | yes |

For both controls, the complete machine `stop` object, UART bytes, and
schema-v5 sidecar are byte-identical to the corresponding automatic-series run.
The complete runner JSON differs only in
`execution_observations_sidecar.path`, which names the new output file. Input
hashes and exact nonce markers match their corresponding source runs.

This is evidence that each observed run outcome repeats under the same
guest-visible nonce and artifacts. Since the automatic N=2 pair differs only
in run-specific nonce/input and output metadata, the cross-run variation is
reproducible per input; attributing the variation specifically to nonce value
is an inference, not a proven mechanism. This control does not classify the
machine or UART differences as benign and does not change the strict comparator.
S5-07 remains blocked/unaccepted.

